From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:03:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: remove parameter-controlled format
 exposure

Remove the inherited multiplanar module parameter. T6040/IMX958 supports normal V4L2 negotiation for contiguous NV12 and P010 through either API, with one memory plane containing the two ISP components. Keep NV12 first and initial; other sensors retain their shipped single-planar API. Do not advertise the old non-contiguous NV12M alias.

Cache complete sensor configuration replies with the video state and print them on the standard log-status ioctl, so collecting the firmware list needs no driver or boot parameter. Free the cache on probe failure and final video release, and test failed discovery without publishing partial state. No module/kernel parameters or platform Kconfig options are added.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
